---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import FreelancerRateTool from '../../components/tools/FreelancerRateTool';
---

<ToolLayout
	title="Freelancer Rate Calculator - Hourly & daily rate estimate | TommyTools"
	description="Free freelancer rate calculator: target income, weeks, billable hours, expenses, and margin → required hourly and daily rates. Planning estimate only - not tax advice."
	heading="Freelancer rate calculator"
	purpose="Estimate the hourly and daily rates you may need to hit a yearly income goal after expenses and an optional reserve. Planning estimate only - not a guarantee of income or a tax calculation."
	category="Business & finance"
	categoryHref="/#cat-business-finance"
>
	<div slot="tool">
		<FreelancerRateTool client:load />
	</div>

	<div slot="instructions">
		<ol>
			<li>Enter your <strong>target annual income</strong> and yearly <strong>business expenses</strong>.</li>
			<li>Set how many <strong>weeks</strong> and <strong>billable hours per week</strong> you expect.</li>
			<li>Optional: add a <strong>reserve / margin %</strong> so rates cover a buffer above income + expenses.</li>
			<li>Read the required billings, hourly rate, daily rate, and margin scenario table.</li>
		</ol>
	</div>

	<div slot="example">
		<p>
			Example: income <strong>60,000</strong>, expenses <strong>8,000</strong>,{' '}
			<strong>48</strong> weeks × <strong>25</strong> billable hours/week, margin{' '}
			<strong>15%</strong>, <strong>5</strong> days/week.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Annual billable hours = 48 × 25 = <strong>1,200</strong></li>
			<li>Required billings = (60,000 + 8,000) / (1 − 0.15) = <strong>80,000</strong></li>
			<li>Hourly rate = 80,000 / 1,200 = <strong>66.67</strong></li>
			<li>Daily rate = 66.67 × (25 / 5) = <strong>333.35</strong></li>
		</ul>
	</div>

	<div slot="formula">
		<ul>
			<li><code>Annual billable hours = Weeks × Billable hours per week</code></li>
			<li>
				<code>Required billings = (Target income + Expenses) / (1 − Margin%)</code>
			</li>
			<li><code>Hourly rate = Required billings / Annual billable hours</code></li>
			<li>
				<code>Daily rate = Hourly rate × (Hours per week / Days per week)</code>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			If margin is 0%, required billings equal income + expenses. Margin must be below 100%.
			Zero billable hours cannot produce a rate.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div slot="limitations">
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Planning estimate only</strong> - not a guarantee of income, and not tax, payroll,
				or legal advice.
			</li>
			<li>Does not model taxes, benefits, unpaid leave, or non-billable admin time beyond what you enter.</li>
			<li>Daily rate assumes billable hours spread evenly across the days/week you set.</li>
			<li>Market rates and utilization vary; treat results as a starting point.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>


	<div slot="related">
		<ul class="related-list">
			<li>
				<a href="/tools/advertising-metrics">Advertising metrics</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="/tools/work-hours">Work hours calculator</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>

</ToolLayout>
